@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
actor "Store Manager" as M
boundary "Report page" as UI
control ReportsController as C
control InventoryReportService as S
participant "IInventoryReportQuery\nEfInventoryReportQuery" as Q
database "SQL Server\nBook + BookStock" as DB
M -> UI : Enter search / in-stock filter
UI -> C : GET /reports/inventory
C -> S : GenerateAsync(filter, ct)
S -> S : Normalize and validate search
S -> Q : ReadAsync(filter, ct)
Q -> DB : One ordered, read-only SQL query
DB --> Q : Book rows + nullable stock
Q --> S : rows
S --> C : InventoryReport(timestamp, rows)
C --> UI : Render table / quantity / unknown count
opt Export current filtered data
 M -> UI : Export CSV
 UI -> C : GET /reports/inventory/export
 C -> S : GenerateAsync(same filter, ct)
 S -> Q : ReadAsync(filter, ct)
 Q -> DB : Read current data
 DB --> Q : rows
 Q --> S : rows
 S --> C : report
 C -> C : InventoryCsv.Export(report)
 C --> UI : UTF-8 CSV download
end
note over M,UI
Implemented as a local Development demo.
Manager authorization is an integration dependency;
this diagram does not claim Login is implemented here.
end note
@enduml
